  "result": "I fixed the help output order. Option names were listed longest prefix first, so `-v, --verbose` showed as `--verbose, -v`. Now short flags come first, as in `-v, --verbose`.\n\nThe cause was one line in `src/click/formatting.py`, in `join_options`. It sorted the option names with `reverse=True`. I removed that, so the sort is now ascending by prefix length.\n\n- **Verification:** the full test suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed, 0 failures). A `--help` run on a sample command now shows `-v, --verbose`.\n- **Regression test:** I added `test_option_help_lists_short_flag_before_long` to `tests/test_formatting.py`.\n- **Line endings:** the working copy uses CRLF, so I matched that in the test file.\n\nNothing is committed. The other ordering I checked is intentional: options follow declaration order, `--help` comes last, and group subcommands are listed alphabetically. If you expected a different order for any of those, tell me which and I'll change it.",
